{"chunk_id": "21f20e26308e", "text": "Maricha warns Ravana that his obsession with Sita will bring ruin. Speaking bitterly yet resignedly, he predicts that Rama will destroy Ravana, Lanka, and the race of titans, and that he himself will die the moment he appears before Rama. Despite knowing the plan is fatal, Maricha agrees to help. Ravana embraces him and carries him in a gem\u2011encrusted flying chariot across forests and kingdoms to Rama\u2019s hermitage in the Dandaka forest. There Ravana orders him to begin the deception. Maricha transforms into a dazzling, supernatural deer\u2014its body glittering with gemlike colors and radiant hues\u2014and wanders near the hermitage to attract Sita\u2019s attention. This moment sets in motion the famous golden-deer illusion that will lure Rama away and enable Sita\u2019s abduction, a pivotal turning point in the epic.\nMaricha reluctantly aids Ravana, transforms into a dazzling golden deer, and wanders near Rama\u2019s hermitage to lure Sita.\nThemes: deception, fatalism, loyalty vs fear, abduction plot, illusion", "vector": [2.6958656235365197e-05, -0.0003790936607401818, 0.0028050807304680347, -0.01817270927131176, -0.02234550006687641, 0.009684409014880657, -0.040558986365795135, -0.03237650915980339, -0.03180563822388649, -0.024479467421770096, 0.022467829287052155, 0.01621543988585472, -0.002509451238438487, 0.01420379988849163, -0.000962494348641485, -0.011397020891308784, 0.04667545482516289, -0.006140255369246006, 0.02733382023870945, -0.021190166473388672, -0.005909188650548458, 0.0029902737587690353, -0.0051786103285849094, 0.0026878484059125185, -0.027388188987970352, 0.017357179895043373, 0.018580473959445953, -0.026300817728042603, 0.004781039897352457, -0.01709892973303795, -0.006463069003075361, -0.022019289433956146, 0.01349021214991808, -0.024615390226244926, -0.035801731050014496, -0.006999959237873554, 0.016419321298599243, -0.005637345835566521, 0.0038125989958643913, -0.01092809159308672, -0.00736015